# PowOS Android: Arch's kwin 6.7.5-3 PKGBUILD + lfdevs's Anland display backend, so KDE Plasma
# can draw on Android through the same display daemon Andromarchy's app hosts.
#
# Upstream recipe: gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/kwin @ 09bed0b (6.7.5-3).
# Patches: github.com/lfdevs/kwin, branch ubuntu/resolute (KWin 6.6.6), debian/patches/:
#   0001, 0002  rebased by us onto 6.7.5 (two hunks did not apply: inputmethod commitText, and the
#               no-DRM dmabuf tranches, which 6.7 restructured around a Q_ASSERT on a scanout device)
#   0003-0007   verbatim
#   0008        ours: the Anland backend ported to KWin 6.7's RenderDevice API, plus a null-DRM
#               guard in core/renderdevice.cpp (see the patch header)
#   0009-0011   ours: phone swipe-up opens the launcher, Android keyboard follows text focus,
#               DPMS wakes when the app comes back to the front
#   0015        ours: ANLAND_SOCKET may be an abstract-namespace socket ("@powos.display", rooted phones)
#   0016        ours: X11 apps' text fields show the Android keyboard (D-Bus SetX11TextFocus, powos-ime-bridge)
#   0017        ours: a full-screen window task keeps its size through output changes (fold) and is scaled to fit
#   0018        ours: floating window tasks resize live ("size"), new windows open as tasks ("export-new"), dialogs
#               drawn into their parent's task, closing a floating task closes its window
#   0019        ours: an Xwayland window is looked at for "export-new" again once it has its wl_surface
#   0020        ours: a touch goes to the task's window or a shown popup/dialog that takes input there (hitTest), not
#               to any helper window whose frame is under it (Steam's); a window that resizes itself is sized back
#   0021        ours: a floating window task's window going full screen by itself tells the app ("fullscreen <id> 1|0"):
#               the same task covers the screen, then floats back; a window that opened full screen floats when it leaves
#   0022        ours: X11 windows a task shows are shown (Mapped, not Kept under KWin's input guard window: Xwayland gave
#               the guard every touch) and raised with their task, so taps reach Steam, its dialogs, any X11 window
#   0023        ours: KWin tells the app its session (a uuid per KWin) and the task ids it has ("session"), also on the
#               app's "hello": the app finishes window tasks of an earlier KWin instead of showing new windows in them
#   0024        ours: an Xwayland window that goes full screen before it has its wl_surface (a game) still opens as a
#               task: one wait per window re-runs the full-screen / new-window decision once the surface is there
#   0025        ours: while the desktop (the Plasma app) is on screen ("desktop 1"), new windows stay KDE windows on it,
#               maximize is KWin's own, and its windows are never pulled out into tasks by "export-new" later
#   0026        ours: KWin tells the app who draws a task's title bar ("decor <id> 1|0": KWin's decoration or the
#               window's own - Steam, GTK header bars - so the app adds no second bar), and a drag on a window's own
#               bar moves the task ("move <id>"), not the window on the hidden desktop
#   0027        ours: a task's window's popups (menus, combo boxes, tooltips) are placed inside the task, not against the
#               output (Workspace::setPopupAreaHandler): past the window's edge they were cut off; desktop windows unchanged
#   0035        ours: the desktop dials a new display daemon after the app restarts (the daemon is the app's child, KWin
#               isn't): an APK update no longer needs a new session; powos-session.sh reattaches instead of restarting
#   0036        ours: a task's window's own maximize/minimize (Steam's client-side bar buttons) are the task's: "maximize"/
#               "minimize <id>" to the app instead of maximizing/unmapping the window on the hidden desktop
#   0037        ours: a fixed-size game window (steam_app_*, min == max: Noita 1280x720) goes full screen in its task, so
#               0032 sizes it to the task on rotate/fold (it stayed small at the task's top left, refusing every resize)
#   0038        ours: "nodecor <id>" from the app: a server-side decorated task window loses KWin's border (noBorder) while
#               it's a task, the frame draws PowOS's bar ("decor" stays 1); restored back on the KWin desktop
#   0039        ours: _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE counts the seat's touch too (a task's touches skip InputRedirection, 0020), so
#               Steam's own header drag starts the move 0026 hands to the task (it was dropped: no button/touch down)
#   0040        ours: a full-screen task's window is never minimized (a Wine/Unity game minimizes itself on focus loss:
#               undone at once), and a floating task gone full screen takes the screen's size at once, not the floating one
#   0041        ours: the consumer's buffers pre-rotated (its surface's transform hint, struct bufs_ext in protocol.h): KWin
#               renders the desktop and task windows already rotated, so SurfaceFlinger needs no GPU rotation on the
#               inner panel (install orientation 270); each frame's render-done byte says the rotation it was drawn with
#   0042        ours: "quit <id>" from the app (the user swiped the task's card / its frame's close): the window is closed
#               (full screen too), and 3 s later a process still running is ended by session/powos-app-quit
#   0043        ours: "ime <id> 1" (cap window-ime): the Android keyboard's show/hide for the focused window goes to its
#               task's own consumer (a web window of home) and its committed text is taken there; "fullscreen <id> 1|0"
#               from the app (cap fullscreen-request) puts the window itself full screen (setFullScreen)
#   0044        ours: "parent <id> <task>" (cap parent) before a new task's "open": another window of the same process
#               has a task (Steam's dialogs have no transient-for), so the app shows the new one with it and in front
#   0045        ours: each consumer buffer's layout (size, stride, offset, format, modifier) logged at info when imported;
#               a warning for a stride under width x 4 or a 90/270 pre-rotated buffer whose width isn't its output's height
#   0050        ours: a task the app quit (0042) says "close <id>" once its window really goes (the task was removed
#               first, so its own close hook never fired: the ship gate's hidden Linux check never saw the close)
#   0051        ours: the Android screen a full-screen task gets (daemon screen, window task buffers) on Xwayland's
#               root as _POWOS_SCREEN_SIZE - unity-screen launches a game at its container's size, not KWin's output
#   0052        ours: a window task draws each frame once (no redraw of a frame already queued: Broforce fps + black
#               flicker); an asked full screen waits for the app's size (no bounce); X11 windows offered by WM_CLASS
#   0053        ours: no GPU (llvmpipe: EGL can't import gralloc buffers, EGL_BAD_ACCESS) - the desktop and window tasks
#               render offscreen and each frame is copied into the mapped consumer buffer (glReadPixels); GPU path unchanged
#   0054        ours (3.63): a keyboard already up moves to a window task's own consumer when the task goes live (its "ime" came
#               first: System Settings' search asked as it opened, the keyboard stayed on the desktop's consumer)
#   0056        ours (3.64): a task's focus makes its window active (a WM_TAKE_FOCUS-only Wine game: a thawed one never was,
#               no input after a resume); a self-minimize undone while live re-activates; a task-shown window's activation
#               never switches to the tasks desktop (Wine 11's _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW requests, workspace.activeWindow)
#   0057        ours (3.65): direct-scanout probe - each window task's 5 s report adds the composite's own CPU/wall ms per
#               frame and how many frames could have gone to the consumer as the client's buffer (fullscreen, one window,
#               linear 1-plane 32-bit dma-buf of the task's size), with the blockers; logs the client buffer's layout
#               (docs/research/window-task-direct-scanout.md). No behaviour change.
#   0058        ours (3.66): direct scanout, step 4 - a window task whose consumer offered it (the app's
#               debug.powos.direct_scanout=1: INPUT_TYPE_DIRECT_CAPS) answers a frame nothing blocks (0057's directBlocker:
#               full screen, one window, linear XR24/AR24 of the task's size) with the client's own dma-buf
#               (FRAME_TAG_DIRECT, fd once per buffer) instead of compositing, holds that buffer until DIRECT_RELEASE,
#               forgets destroyed buffers, composites any other frame. Without the consumer's caps: unchanged.
#   0059        ours (3.67): the desktop's reconnect never waits on KWin's thread - try_exit_fallback() asked the daemon
#               for a consumer and poll()ed up to 100 ms for it on every 200 ms tick, for as long as the desktop had none
#               (behind every full-screen game task): KWin's main thread stopped half the time and the game's frame
#               callbacks came ~100 ms late 4-5x/s (Xwayland's 100 ms frame timeouts, Broforce p95 104 ms). Now it asks
#               once (the daemon keeps the request until a consumer deposits its fds), never waits, and a QSocketNotifier
#               on ctrl_fd in fallback wakes the reconnect when the answer comes; redial's answer likewise.
#
# HACK: same pkgname as Arch's kwin with pkgrel 3.1 (makepkg allows only integer[.integer]; ".1" = ours), so every Plasma package's
# "depends=(kwin)" is satisfied by ours and pacman sees it as newer than 6.7.5-3. The real fix is
# getting the Anland backend upstream into KWin; until then each Plasma update means rebasing
# these patches and bumping pkgver here (the rootfs build pins kwin so -Syu can't replace it).

pkgname=kwin
pkgver=6.7.5
_dirver=$(echo $pkgver | cut -d. -f1-3)
pkgrel=3.67
pkgdesc='An easy to use, but flexible, Wayland compositor (PowOS: Anland backend for Android)'
arch=(aarch64)
url='https://kde.org/plasma-desktop/'
license=(LGPL-2.0-or-later)
depends=(aurorae breeze glibc iio-sensor-proxy plasma-activities kauth kcmutils kcolorscheme kconfig
